-# McSH (aka. McShell)
+# HelioMC
 
-![McSH Launcher](assets/banner.png)
+**HelioMC** (CLI: `helio`) is a terminal Minecraft launcher built for people
+who want to manage Minecraft without a GUI. No Electron, no splash screens, no
+background services — just a shell prompt.
 
-**A fast, lightweight Minecraft launcher for the terminal.**
+HelioMC is an unofficial fork of [McSH](https://github.com/kalakaritzu/mcsh),
+rebranded and extended with native [Ely.by](https://ely.by) account support
+(browser OAuth + authlib-injector).
 
-**Website:** https://mcsh.dev
+## Highlights
 
-McSH is a CLI Minecraft launcher built for people who want to manage Minecraft without the overhead of a GUI. No Electron, no splash screens, no background services. Just a shell prompt.
+- **Ely.by OAuth** — `helio auth elyby` signs in through your browser using the
+  device-code flow. No password is entered in the launcher.
+- **Modpack support** — search and install modpacks from Modrinth.
+- **Mod management** — install, update, enable/disable, and profile mods.
+- **Mod loaders** — Vanilla, Fabric, Forge, NeoForge, and Quilt.
+- **Instances** — separate versions, mods, worlds, RAM, and window settings.
+- **Managed Java** — downloads the right JDK automatically when needed.
+- **Orange by default** — the `helio` theme uses an orange accent, with six
+  additional themes available.
+- **Quick launch** — `helio run <name>` starts an instance without the REPL.
 
